Common reqs, because computers demand tribute:

    Linux x86 or x86_64 with 32-bit ELF support
    alsa-utils, /bin/aplay is the band
    SDL2 runtime for framebuffer-emulator

The release contains two 1K demo binaries:

    wilma-emulator  writes /tmp/fb0 for the included framebuffer-emulator
    wilma-nativefb  writes a real /dev/fb0

Party-safe desktop route (recommended):

    ./framebuffer-emulator --demo ./wilma-emulator

Native framebuffer tribute:

    ./wilma-nativefb

The native version needs a 1024x768x32 framebuffer. Put something like
this in /etc/default/grub:

    GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT="video=1024x768-32"

Source lives in src/ for the 1K creature and fbe/ for its SDL2 terrarium.
Convenient source rituals:

    cd src
    make release
    make run-emulator
    make run-emulator FBE_ARGS="--display 1"
    make run-emulator FBE_ARGS="--windowed"
    make run-native

Build tribute (debnish):

    dpkg --add-architecture i386
    apt update
    apt install make nasm gcc-multilib binutils python3 libc6:i386 libc6-dev-i386 libsdl2-dev alsa-utils

If the terminal becomes modern art, type reset blindly and press Enter.

